--- a/jails/instances/lab-claude/README.org
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-claude/README.org
@@ -34,3 +34,17 @@ message goes to no one; fix the address and send again. A non-zero
 exit can also mean Fastmail refused the message or could not be
 reached; msmtp prints the server's reply either way. Nothing is
 queued, so a message that failed was not sent.
+
+* packages
+The jail's packages are the ones listed in =instance.conf=. When the
+agent needs one more, it can install it from FreeBSD-ports without a
+rebuild:
+#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
+doas /usr/local/sbin/pkg-install-ports jq
+#+END_EXAMPLE
+
+doas allows claude to run that script as root and nothing else. The
+script only runs =pkg install -r FreeBSD-ports=, so it cannot remove
+packages, change repositories, or install into another root. A
+package installed this way is lost when the jail is rebuilt; it
+belongs in =instance.conf= too.
